| Feature                             | `@Value`                            | `@ConfigurationProperties`                                   |
| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Purpose**                         | Inject a *single value*             | Bind a *group of related values*                             |
| **Target**                          | Field or method parameter           | Entire POJO (class with fields)                              |
| **Prefix support**                  | ❌ None                              | ✅ Yes (`prefix = "app"`)                                     |
| **Type-safety**                     | ❌ Manual casting                    | ✅ Automatic (based on field types)                           |
| **Default values**                  | ✅ Easy (`@Value("${key:default}")`) | ✅ Possible via defaults in fields                            |
| **Complex/nested config**           | ❌ Harder                            | ✅ Supported                                                  |
| **Validation support**              | ❌ No                                | ✅ Can use `@Validated`, `@NotNull`, etc.                     |
| **Recommended for**                 | Few properties                      | Many grouped properties                                      |
| **Spring Boot feature integration** | Basic                               | Works well with YAML, `@EnableConfigurationProperties`, etc. |

| Annotation        | Used for                        | HTTP Method               | Typical Purpose       |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------- | --------------------- |
| `@RequestMapping` | Generic mapping (any HTTP type) | GET / POST / PUT / DELETE | General use, flexible |
| `@GetMapping`     | Read data                       | GET                       | Fetch / display info  |
| `@PostMapping`    | Send data                       | POST                      | Create / submit data  |

| Action              | HTTP Method | Annotation       | Meaning                   |
| ------------------- | ----------- | ---------------- | ------------------------- |
| You open the form   | `GET`       | `@GetMapping`    | Show the page (read data) |
| You submit the form | `POST`      | `@PostMapping`   | Save data to the server   |
| You delete an item  | `DELETE`    | `@DeleteMapping` | Remove data               |
| You update an item  | `PUT`       | `@PutMapping`    | Update existing data      |




| Feature              | `@Query`                             | `@Modifying`                                           |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Purpose**          | Used for custom **SELECT** queries   | Used for **UPDATE**, **DELETE**, or **INSERT** queries |
| **Return Type**      | Entities, DTOs, lists, scalar values | `int` (affected rows) or `void`                        |
| **Transactional?**   | Not required (read-only)             | ✅ Required (write operation)                           |
| **Default behavior** | Executes JPQL or SQL select          | Executes modifying query                               |
| **Used together?**   | `@Query` alone                       | `@Query` + `@Modifying` together                       |

| Annotation      | Used In    | Extracts value from | Example URL     | Example Code                          |
| --------------- | ---------- | ------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| `@PathVariable` | Controller | Path segment        | `/users/101`    | `@GetMapping("/{id}")`                |
| `@RequestParam` | Controller | Query string        | `/users?id=101` | `@GetMapping` + `@RequestParam("id")` |
| `@Param`        | Repository | JPA query parameter | —               | `@Query("... WHERE field = :param")`  |

| Concept             | Used for                                                           | Example URL                  | Meaning                                              |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| **`@PathVariable`** | **Building the URL path itself** (to identify a specific resource) | `/users/101`                 | “Get me the user whose ID is 101”                    |
| **`@RequestParam`** | **Passing query parameters** (to filter, sort, or modify results)  | `/users?role=admin&sort=asc` | “Get me all users with role admin, sorted ascending” |


| Feature                      | `@Valid`                                            | `@Validated`                                                            |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Belongs to**               | `jakarta.validation.Valid` (JSR-303 standard)       | `org.springframework.validation.annotation.Validated` (Spring-specific) |
| **Used for**                 | Validating simple objects (mainly DTOs or entities) | Validating objects **and** validation **groups**                        |
| **Group Validation Support** | ❌ Not supported                                     | ✅ Supported                                                             |
| **Where usable**             | On method params, fields, or nested objects         | On class, method, or interface (method-level validation)                |
| **Typical use**              | In `@RequestBody` inside controller                 | On entire controller class or service for method-level validation       |
